# JavaScript and TypeScript Common Native API

The host declares `source.tenant_field` once in its native domain and binds
trusted context once with `Engine.configure(domain, adapter).withTenant(8)`. Ordinary assignments omit the matching
tenant. Reads, fluent writes, actions and callback engines inherit the binding.

This notebook inspects and executes the complete native program on in-memory
SQLite. Install the native repository's pinned development environment first.
Set `SELECTO_TYPESCRIPT_PATH` if the checkout is not a sibling of
`selecto_livebooks`. Verified native source: `484e8a8e24b2ffbfbb2b3631d1c89e7efd58d261`.

## Inspect The Native Program

```elixir
repo = System.get_env("SELECTO_TYPESCRIPT_PATH") || Path.expand("../../selecto-typescript", __DIR__)
IO.puts(File.read!(Path.join(repo, "examples/common-native-api.mjs")))
```

The sample declares a native domain structure, previews actual SQL and separate
parameters, inserts without `org_id`, then invokes the archive action inside an
inherited transaction. A second callback inserts another row and attempts a
refused foreign-tenant delete. That callback rolls back its preceding insert.
Final scoped rows are `[[2, 8, "Test", "archived"]]`.

## Execute And Verify

```elixir
mise = System.find_executable("mise") || raise "mise executable is required"
{build_output, build_status} = System.cmd(mise, ["exec", "--", "npm", "run", "build"], cd: repo, stderr_to_stdout: true)
IO.puts(build_output)
if build_status != 0, do: raise "Native JavaScript build failed"
{output, status} = System.cmd(mise, ["exec", "--", "node", "examples/common-native-api.mjs"], cd: repo, stderr_to_stdout: true)
IO.puts(output)
if status != 0 or not String.contains?(output, "PASS: JavaScript common native API"), do: raise "Native JavaScript sample failed"
```

The SQLite insert preview binds `[2, "Test", "done", 8]` to four `?` placeholders. The tenant
stays in SQL even though the calling code omits it. Native permissions,
cardinality, returning, conflict identities and scope rules remain authoritative.
Each action invocation plans and authorizes its own phase; preview never grants
execution authority. Independently scoped root and site columns keep separate
values.

Callbacks await sequential operations on one retained connection; SQLite and PostgreSQL adapters opt in. Nested work uses native savepoints, host transactions retain ownership and callback engines expire on completion. Streaming refuses inside callbacks.

Run `npm run check` in the native checkout for the release gate. Configure its disposable
PostgreSQL integration/observer URLs to enable live service checks. These checks
do not claim live coverage of every other provider or every related read path.
